# routine — nothing is learned where the player has no business standing
#
# Standing in a private area is trespass: every act there is a crime (Verb.IsIllegal), the narration
# header says ◆ TRESPASSING ◆, and no routine is learned — one would be a standing invitation back,
# walked with none of the risk. All three read the one test, PrivacyModel.IsTrespassing.
#
# The test location's back room is private, reached from the public hall by an unlocked door. Walk
# through it and leave from inside: in public ground that would teach a Go to routine; here it must
# teach nothing.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "Test Room Door"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# The hall is public.
expect-state where trespass=no
expect open ground

strategy succeed
goal open_door
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb open_door
expect Moved to:

observe none
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180

# The room is not.
expect-state where Test Room
expect-state where trespass=yes
expect TRESPASSING

# The weaver lives in that room, so the footer is RUNAWAY rather than LEAVE — an escape roll, which
# `strategy succeed` lets through. The visit then ends from inside the room.
click button
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
wait mode WorldView 90

inspect routines
expect-no-state routines category=goto
quit
